{#- macros/key_remove.j2 -- the DECLARED key-removal fixture operation of the isolated-case instrument (C1;
    codex-tick328-329 missing_keys: null / malformed values never replace actual MISSING-key coverage). A case
    overlay is combine(recursive=True) and can therefore never delete a key; this macro is the one declared way a
    case removes keys, from its OWN isolated copy only (one_case.yml confines the target to an admitted copied file,
    records its exact pre/post bytes and proves every removed key absent before the probe). It is fixture data
    handling, not a second desired-state engine: production merge semantics are untouched and the source tree is
    never read or written here. STATUS: UNEXECUTED (authored; reviewed and run through the declared runner only).
    Template vars:
      op    -- 'present' | 'remove'
      doc   -- the parsed isolated copy (a mapping)
      paths -- the declared canonical key paths, each a NON-EMPTY list of non-empty string segments from the
               document root (a list, never a dotted string: a key may itself contain '.')
    Output JSON:
      op present -> {"present": [<bool per declared path, in declared order>]}: true iff every parent is a
                    mapping carrying the next segment and the leaf key exists (its value may be anything, null too)
      op remove  -> {"doc": <doc rebuilt without exactly the declared leaf keys>}: every other key and value is
                    carried unchanged (serialized with to_json; the CALLER refuses a document whose JSON round
                    trip is not lossless, so no key/value type can change silently).
    A path whose parent chain is absent is simply not rebuilt (the caller has already refused it through op
    present); nothing is created. -#}
{%- macro has(node, p) -%}
{%- if node is mapping and p[0] in node -%}
{{- has(node[p[0]], p[1:]) if (p | length) > 1 else 'y' -}}
{%- else -%}
{{- 'n' -}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro strip(node, ps) -%}
{%- set ns = namespace(parts=[]) -%}
{%- for k in node -%}
{%- set ks = namespace(drop=false, sub=[]) -%}
{%- for p in ps -%}
{%- if p[0] == k -%}
{%- if (p | length) == 1 -%}
{%- set ks.drop = true -%}
{%- else -%}
{%- set ks.sub = ks.sub + [p[1:]] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if not ks.drop -%}
{%- set ns.parts = ns.parts + [(k | to_json) ~ ':' ~ ((strip(node[k], ks.sub) if (ks.sub and node[k] is mapping) else (node[k] | to_json)))] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- '{' ~ (ns.parts | join(',')) ~ '}' -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- if op == 'present' -%}
{%- set ps = namespace(v=[]) -%}
{%- for p in paths -%}
{%- set ps.v = ps.v + [has(doc, p) == 'y'] -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- {'present': ps.v} | to_json -}}
{%- elif op == 'remove' -%}
{{- '{"doc":' ~ strip(doc, paths) ~ '}' -}}
{%- else -%}
{{- {'error': 'op must be present or remove'} | to_json -}}
{%- endif -%}
